    "field": "Vegetation-climate feedbacks",
    "problem": "Existing climate change models have not incorporated feedbacks from changes in vegetation structure, which can modify land surface characteristics and significantly alter climate predictions by partially offsetting the effects of known physiological responses.",
    "method": "We propose a method that iteratively couples a general circulation model with an equilibrium vegetation model to quantify the effects of both physiological and structural vegetation feedbacks on climate simulations under a doubled carbon dioxide scenario.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the effects of both physiological and structural vegetation feedbacks on a doubled-CO2 climate using a general circulation model coupled with an equilibrium vegetation model to assess their contrasting impacts on climate simulations.",
    "model": [
        "GCM",
        "Sheffield University vegetation model"
    ],
